<title>USA: Willis Finance sees gain from credit pact.</title>
<headline>Willis Finance sees gain from credit pact.</headline>
<dateline>SAUSALITO, Calif. 1997-02-19</dateline>
<text>
<p>Willis Lease Finance Corp on Wednesday said an unnamed U.S. financial institution would provide the company with a new $41.5 million credit line, replacing an existing bank loan and resulting in a net first-quarter gain of $3.1 million, or $.55 per share.</p>
<p>The new credit line will increase incremental interest expense by about $450,000 in 1997, while saving almost $1 million in interest over 10 years because of a shorter repayment schedule, the company said.</p>
</text>
